{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Completion verifier FAIL was valid and identified two test-only gaps after the production change landed: reachable-absent was not asserted false in the named unit proving file, and no explicit wiring oracle pinned all four consumers to the shared probe. Added reachable-absent and unreachable false cases plus an exact four-consumer shared-probe test that forbids a second ls-remote path. Mutation evidence: bypassing the shared probe and returning true made both the negative control and wiring test fail. Production code remains identical to landed main; sending this test-only completion patch through Gerrit before re-verifying."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785636766263747001,"uuid":"3c0bfe36-2f09-4940-b718-789df3a9a286"}